  "description": "The cache entry for **http://example.com/resource** is stored under **/var/cache/dir1/object123.dat** with an ETag of **\"abc123def\"** and a Cache\u2011Control directive of **max-age=3600**. The object resides on disk (**cacheindisk\u202f=\u202fYES**) but not in memory (**cacheinmemory\u202f=\u202fNO**) nor in secondary storage (**cacheinsecondary\u202f=\u202fNO**). Its original URL list is recorded as **cacheurls\u202f=\u202fhttp://example.com/resource**, and the cached file is identified as a base file (**cachecellbasefile\u202f=\u202fYES**) without application\u2011firewall metadata (**cachecellappfwmetadataexists\u202f=\u202fNO**) and not marked as a complex object (**cachecellcomplex\u202f=\u202fNO**). Compression is applied in **gzip** format, and the object uses HTTP/1.1 (**cachecellhttp11\u202f=\u202fYES**) with a weak ETag (**cachecellweaketag\u202f=\u202fYES**) but no strong tag inserted (**cachecelletaginserted\u202f=\u202fNO**). The response metadata shows a size of **2048\u202fbytes** (**cacheressize**) and a header size of **512\u202fbytes** (**cachereshdrsize**), with a response date of **2023-07-01T12:34:56Z** and a last\u2011modified header of **Tue, 01 Jul 2023 12:34:56 GMT**.\n\nOperational statistics indicate a total of **1\u202f234 hits** (**cachecellhits**) and **210 misses** (**cachecellmisses**), with the minimum hit threshold set to **5** (**cachecellminhit**) but the min\u2011hit flag currently **NO** (**cachecellminhitflag**). At the moment there are **45 downstream hits** (**cachecelldhits**) and **12 current misses** (**cachecellcurmisses**) being served to **3 readers** (**cachecellcurreaders**). The request and response processing times are **150\u202fms** (**cachecellreqtime**) and **200\u202fms** (**cachecellrestime**) respectively, and the object is verified at its destination IP (**cachecelldestipverified\u202f=\u202fYES**) with a destination address of **192.168.1.10:80**. The object\u2019s expiration timestamp is **1622548800** seconds since epoch (**cachecellexpires**) with millisecond precision **1622548800123** (**cachecellexpiresmillisec**), and its current age is **300\u202fseconds** (**cachecurage**). The marker reason for any special handling is **\u201cWaiting for min hit\u201d**, and marker\u2011related flags such as **ignoremarkerobjects** and **includenotreadyobjects** are both **OFF**. The object is not flagged for flushing (**flushed\u202f=\u202fNO**) and is not a firewall\u2011proxy object (**cachecellfwpxyobj\u202f=\u202fNO**).\n\nThe entry belongs to **group\u202f=\u202fgroup1** (display name **Group One**) within **contentgroup\u202f=\u202fgroupA**, and is associated with **policy\u202f=\u202f5** named **Policy1** on node **42**. It is served on port **8080** and identified by locator **1001** (both **locator** and **locatorshow**). Prefetching is enabled (**prefetch\u202f=\u202fYES**) with a period of **60\u202fseconds** (**prefetchperiod**) or **60\u202f000\u202fms** (**prefetchperiodmillisec**). The cache rule applied is of type **cache** with the action **store**, and the selector used is **selectorA** with value **valA**. No HTTP callout cell is used (**httpcalloutcell\u202f=\u202fNO**), but the callout named **callout1** succeeded (**httpcalloutresult\u202f=\u202fSUCCESS**). The request was a **GET** (**httpmethod**) that returned HTTP status **200** (both **httpstatus** and **httpstatusoutput**). The return type for the query is **BOOL**, and there are **10 total objects** (**totalobjs**) with no warning bucket skips (**warnbucketskip\u202f=\u202f0**). Hit parameters include **paramA\u202f=\u202fvalueA**, and hit values contain **value1\u202f=\u202f123**.",
